#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:6
msgid "What Is Macro Hygiene"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:8
msgid ""
"A macro systems is said to be **hygienic** if macros defined with it cannot "
"accidentally capture or shadow identifiers from their expansion sites."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:11
msgid ""
"This is desirable because it helps reason about macros separately from their "
"uses, avoiding bugs when code invoking macros might unintentionally use the "
"same identifier used internally by a macro."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:15
msgid ""
"Macros in C and C++ using the C preprocessor are not hygienic, but Rust's "
"macro system implements a limited form of hygiene."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:18
msgid ""
"Macro hygiene imposes two restrictions, corresponding to the two directions "
"of influence between the macro's and the calling code's lexical environment."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:21
msgid "A macro system is **unhygienic** if a macro can either:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:23
msgid "Implicitly access identifiers in the surrounding callsite scope."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:24
msgid ""
"Define a new local identifier that bleeds out and is implicitly accessible "
"by the code surrounding its callsite."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:27
msgid "Example 1: Implicitly Accessing Calling Environment (Unhygienic)"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:32
msgid "// Unhygienic: attempts to implicitly read `local` from callsite\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:33
#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:55
msgid "\"{}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:38
#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:49
msgid "\"Hello, Macros!\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:39
#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:55
msgid "// In an unhygienic system, this would compile!\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:43
msgid "Example 2: Leaking Local Variables (Unhygienic)"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:48
msgid "// Unhygienic: intent is to leak `local` to callsite\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:59
msgid ""
"In Rust, **neither of these examples compile**. Both produce the error: "
"`error[E0425]: cannot find value 'local' in this scope`."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:62
msgid ""
"Rust's macro system treats variables hygienically, protecting from silent "
"namespace pollution."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md:65
msgid "However, declarative macros in Rust are not fully hygienic!"
msgstr ""
